WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.200
How can we add a half and a quarter when

2
00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:03.900
their pieces are different sizes?

3
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.200
Start with the same-sized whole.

4
00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:07.840
First, try equal parts.

5
00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.560
Two sevenths plus three sevenths makes

6
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:11.460
five sevenths.

7
00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:12.860
We count the parts.

8
00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.080
Their size stays the same, so the

9
00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:16.300
denominator stays seven.

10
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:18.880
For one half plus one quarter, rename

11
00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:19.320
the half.

12
00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.640
Split each half into two equal pieces.

13
00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.220
One half is two quarters.

14
00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:25.620
Now add two quarters and one quarter.

15
00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.060
That makes three quarters.

16
00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:29.500
Do not add the denominators: we are

17
00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:30.620
still counting quarters.

18
00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:33.160
Subtraction uses equal-sized parts too.

19
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.540
Take three quarters minus one eighth.

20
00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:37.880
Each quarter is two eighths, so three

21
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:39.220
quarters is six eighths.

22
00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:40.460
Remove one eighth.

23
00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:41.720
Five eighths remain.

24
00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:44.300
On a number line, start at six eighths

25
00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:45.720
and jump back one eighth.

26
00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.420
Sometimes we can simplify.

27
00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:49.740
One sixth plus three sixths is four

28
00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:50.180
sixths.

29
00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:52.460
Divide the numerator and denominator by

30
00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:52.720
two.

31
00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:55.020
Four sixths equals two thirds.

32
00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:57.120
With mixed numbers, keep track of the

33
00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:57.520
wholes.

34
00:00:57.980 --> 00:00:59.880
One and four fifths plus two fifths is

35
00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:00.860
one and six fifths.

36
00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:03.160
Five fifths make another whole, so the

37
00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:04.560
answer is two and one fifth.

38
00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:06.580
You can use more than two fractions.

39
00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:09.300
One half plus one quarter minus one

40
00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:11.600
eighth becomes four eighths plus two

41
00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:12.860
eighths minus one eighth.

42
00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:14.660
The answer is five eighths.

43
00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:17.820
Your turn: two thirds minus one sixth.

44
00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:19.040
Pause and think.

45
00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:20.940
Two thirds is four sixths.

46
00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.260
Subtract one sixth to get three sixths,

47
00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:24.640
which is one half.

48
00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:27.340
Remember: use the same whole, rename

49
00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:30.320
into equal-sized parts, calculate, then

50
00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:31.520
simplify if you can.
